    "file_name": "AFP_ENG_19970407.0528.tml",
    "doc_text": "AFP_ENG_19970407.0528\n\nWASHINGTON, April 7 , 1997 (AFP)\n\nUS wants to meet Palestinians on Mideast peace\n\n\n\n\nPresident Bill Clinton said Monday the United States would talk next with the Palestinians about re-starting the Mideast peace process after he met Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu.\n\n\"We had a very specific, frank, candid and long talk,\" Clinton told reporters following his two-hour meeting at the White House with the Israeli leader.\n\n\"It was a long and very thorough meeting ... now it's important for us to visit with the Palestinians,\" Clinton said, adding he would do his best to get Israeli-Palestinian negotiations back on track.\n\nClinton declined to give details on the substance of his meeting with Netanyahu.",
